Here is the commit message:
AMBARI-22517. NPE during Ambari schema upgrade while updating
 Hive configs.

Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by a NullPointerException (NPE) that occurred during the Ambari schema upgrade when attempting to access properties of the `hsiSiteConfig` object without checking if it was null. If `hsiSiteConfig` was not found (i.e., it was null), the subsequent call to `hsiSiteConfig.getProperties()` would lead to an NPE, disrupting the upgrade process.

Here is the patch:

   protected void updateHiveConfigs() throws AmbariException {
